From b44079bea7d3dd8cccfe19e6304464556bcc0f08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eileenthg <40307498+eileenthg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 23:59:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] Fix Registry.getValue->get rename and redesign
 MobEffect helpers around Holder<MobEffect>

- Registry#getValue(ResourceLocation) was renamed to get(ResourceLocation) in 1.21
  (getKey/containsKey unchanged); fixed every BuiltInRegistries.*.getValue( call across
  Util.java, Modid.java, ModEvents.java. Registry#containsValue was removed outright;
  Util.rl(ItemLike) now uses getResourceKey(T).isPresent() to check registration instead.
- MobEffectInstance's constructors need Holder<MobEffect> now, and vanilla MobEffects.* backup
  constants (MobEffects.REGENERATION, MobEffects.DIG_SPEED, etc.) are themselves already
  Holder<MobEffect> - incompatible with the old MobEffect... vararg parameters throughout
  Util.effect/Modid.effect/Modid.effectInstance/Util.addEffect. Redesigned that whole chain to
  work in Holder<MobEffect> end to end instead of patching every call site individually, and
  updated the ~9 small compat effect-getter classes that fed into it (TeaCompat,
  ExquisitoCompat, CosmopolitanCompat, SOBCompat, NeapolitanCompat, BrewinChewinCompat,
  AtmosphericCompat, UnusualEndCompat, ArsNouveauCompat, UndergardenCompat,
  NecroniumKnifeItem) to return/consume Holder<MobEffect> to match.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
